oLtV1bIgIwL3kBuIsn3dmxa3nQUt_u310euQitarwInWMiPadJ-UhUA-ezmB75481vkSERr2Fz7Yp0XhcxCFV10fqP8K00maYx6ZoAy0mFCY4H0qvfIlleiAmu0ptHdePBhXIxUOEW-hWC_QkkwV5mZcYvQ2oA4La6EbODIcliFCBCV402-dqBdiMz1gMzrwVzoVV9Khg2ZAAeO7Wxdq-ALdUx5bSkXoW7gMKTNxoLHm_pegYcHu8VtBB8m7tzpyoMRjLz-cHy8xDS8tl9QcCBJs12uFJ6iUq5LMfPbJP6d25z_b_2xnzhugPbXTZPDCdoK82jHPx0WtVHbKjsCfsakDk9gUbbCyEWKafTQaaipcBf2C7i87Q_UV0nwSAmo8zpYwGmFTaqn8IudYD9Xn8djgyityBFHeMzxCIsfDjQo-R7GxJoGsfwktzveRKNbt3h2fLaqEJGIvzCvXpb73FLvRiSkD4uECOrIZP2vVjEzBZ2s0FuXMWg74aJIyU374qKW4aav4whMWbXw8T0WXKki6ajxYxUCjqQjZ_cibUxtpyoU9rZuFOtohAkwvvx2H-N91JW5fycgEFhr3rkc-CtxMtETkzo1sJ2enq_V6evovX3bQLKW4JrK8UymaZP31iP0FVfxZr9aXAD9LLbR8oLOpg44vHEuQ="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0605e517a21a474d016ae20fcbfbe08191a4fd20bf7a91b8fd","call_id":"call_e76d9c76b646432383c221ad7672065b","name":"record_author_checks","arguments":"{\"candidate\":7,\"readiness\":\"no_known_issue\",\"open_issues\":[],\"resolutions\":[],\"original_context_note\":\"Compared spec.full_target with target-selection.json/full_target and problem.md:16-41: the full selected text is retained exactly, including arbitrary admissible M, integer 0≤λ<p, every prime p, arbitrary characteristic-p field K, λ=0 and p=2, and both nonzeroness and the invariant-subspace alternative. H001-H004 retain all original givens at their stated origins. All four H nodes are used; within H002 the original irreducibility/highest-weight designation is retained although the actual calculation only needs the given dimension, commutators, and H003. No optional proof phase or material calculation was omitted. R001-R005 correspond to the five supplied phases, with the rational tensor rank-one calculation n=nr retained in R003/S003, rather than assuming a submodule of C has rank one. D001-D005 and D014-D015 fix all index, factorial, divided-power and binomial conventions, including empty products. D007's ring structure is grounded by prime p in H001; D008 defines the image R-span, and R002 proves its identification with the original R⊗_Z M before the tensor identification is used. D009 is guarded by N001 and H001 in every using packet; no basis property is obtained merely from the definition. D010-D011 are inverse-image submodules, with their equality, finite generation and principality proved in R003. D012 defines the tensor object without assuming nonzeroness; lattice preservation is proved in R004/S001 from H002,H004. D013 preserves the abstract rank-three Chevalley form, not its operator image, including the trivial representation. Its H002,H004 guards are direct in R005. The eight selected library contracts were compared with successful pinned probes and the relevant source readbacks: M001 baseChange_apply includes the scalar-extension basis and all semiring/module/algebra premises; M002 includes strong rank condition; M003 includes finite dimension, independence and the cardinal equality; M004 includes the full localized-module predicate and localization premises; M005 is invariant finrank under linear equivalence; M006 requires free finite components; M007 is the prime factorial equivalence; M008 supplies freeness over a division ring. M004 correctly uses an endomorphism semiring in its general statement. The failed guessed namespace for M003 was not retained, and M006 selects the successfully probed dependent-product theorem, not the earlier scalar-valued pi theorem. Humphreys is the provenance of the supplied exercise, not an imported E theorem used as a proof premise, so no unavailable external theorem is assumed. All selected M and all N lie in P's AND closure, each N/P has its unique producer, and no unverified source or extra H is present. This is my same-author closing inspection, not independent Audit A or a claim that structural checking proves the mathematics.\",\"output_notes\":[{\"id\":\"N001\",\"note\":\"Checked N001 against R001/S001-S003: both commutator inductions are stated for their full natural ranges; the nonzero string calculation includes i=0, polynomial isolation gives independence over C, and M003 plus the exact dimension gives a basis. The absent h-eigenvalue argument proves y^{λ+1}v=0 only in characteristic zero. The exported x,y,h matrices, both divided-power binomial coefficients, termination conditions and integral coefficients agree with the iteration and finite counting argument in S003. Consumers receive the basis and formulas explicitly, not an equation label.\"},{\"id\":\"N002\",\"note\":\"R002/S001 proves the canonical tensor multiplication isomorphism and I-indexed basis, while S002 proves preservation by every divided power. S003 tests every basis vector to give all three projector identities, and S004 proves the binomial is an R-unit before dividing. The resulting full E_ij formula and preservation assertion are exported. In the statement a_R is R-valued and r is the natural divided-power index, so the two distinct scalar domains are not conflated.\"},{\"id\":\"N003\",\"note\":\"R003/F001 exports equal coordinate modules, nonzeroness, finite generation and the direct decomposition. S002 proves the exact multiplication-map injection from the localized-module source, and S003 proves its tensor dimension is one by n=nr with n>0. S004-S006 construct the nonzero generator b from rational coefficients and the minimum p-exponent. S006 proves the basis property and explicitly explains why it applies to every nonzero generator of J, matching both the existential and universal clauses of N003.\"},{\"id\":\"N004\",\"note\":\"R004/S001-S002 prove the scalar map and both natural scalar-extension identifications with actual maps and inverse checks. S003 proves that the scalar extensions of b e_i form the claimed K-basis, including the reduction through F_p, and computes all three generator matrices. S004 grounds every factorial inverse by 0≤r≤λ<p and every binomial inverse by the R-unit property, then exports the complete matrix-unit formula and its subspace-invariance consequence. Thus R005 needs no unexported choice of b or producer-side tensor identification.\"},{\"id\":\"P\",\"note\":\"R005/S001 establishes nonzeroness by β_0 with 0∈I, independently of W. S001-S002 treat both zero and nonzero subspaces and use ε_ij w=c_jβ_i to obtain every basis vector in W. S003 discharges invariance and quantifies W, then identifies invariance under the abstract Chevalley algebra with invariance under x,y,h by its generator span. This gives the exact nonzero irreducibility target over arbitrary K, including λ=0 and p=2.\"}],\"inference_notes\":[{\"id\":\"R001\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the actual R001 packet. S001 uses H001 for the index range and H002,H003 for the two inductions; their displayed base and successor calculations are valid for all natural indices. The repeated x calculation has nonzero factors for 0≤i≤λ, including the empty product. In S002 L1 is precisely the test relation, is discharged after coefficient isolation, and no characteristic-p eigenvalue claim is made. F001 and H002 ground the source application and the terminal y-string argument. S003 uses F001,F002 to derive all generator and divided-power coefficients; D014-D015 and the ordered-subset count establish the factorial/binomial normalization rather than assuming integrality. Each direct input has that actual role; no producer or non-input H is needed.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M003 at S002 is instantiated with scalar field C, vector space V, finite index I, family e. H002 gives finite dimension λ+1, H001 and D001-D002 give card(I)=λ+1, and the polynomial isolation earlier in S002 proves independence. The source conclusion is exactly span_C(e)=V; combining it with the already proved independence gives the asserted basis, without claiming more from M003.\",\"declaration_check\":\"Checked D001-D005,D014-D015, local induction index t and relation family c against their S scopes. The remaining indices in the formulas are explicitly quantified or finite-product/sum-bound; the auxiliary A≥r in S003 is the natural counting parameter local to that calculation. The complex factorial denominators are nonzero finite products, so e,X,Y are defined before their use. L1 does not escape the independence proof; all exported indices are rebound in N001.\"},{\"id\":\"R002\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R002 using only H001,H004,N001 and its three library inputs. S001 takes the common integer/complex basis from H004, its finiteness from the finite complex basis N001, and uses scalar extension plus complex independence to prove the canonical tensor embedding, not to assume it. F001 grounds the image and span assertions; H004 grounds F002 for all natural divided powers. Testing N001's explicit coefficients gives F003 with the correct order Y_λX_λ and X_{λ-i} on the left. S004 divides only after establishing unit denominators and then uses R-module closure. The finite basis choices are eliminated in the basis-existence conclusion, so no extra witness assumption escapes.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M001 at S001 uses Z→R and the integer basis m of M from H004. Its basis vectors 1⊗m_a map to m_a, which are R-independent by their given complex independence and span the image by D008. The two actual M002 instances at S001 compare the complex bases m and e of V, giving card(A)=dim_C V=card(I)=n; C is a field and has strong rank condition. M007 at S004 is used with prime p and d=λ,j,λ-j, all natural and <p from H001 and j∈I; hence each factorial has an inverse in R, giving the binomial unit by its factorial quotient. Every source condition has these packet-local grounds.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The local finite index A and common basis m are chosen from H004 together with N001's finite basis and live through S002 only. Qop is the explicitly defined product Y_λX_λ in S003-S004, not the target node P. E is only used with direct N001 and H001, satisfying D009's construction guard. All E indices are in I, and every divided-power index λ-i or λ-j is a natural number. The output map's R-scalar a_R is distinct from the natural index r.\"},{\"id\":\"R003\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected the full R003 packet, in particular the arbitrary-lattice rank step. S001 uses N002's actual matrix-unit preservation and N001's basis to prove F001; projection of a finite basis proves finite generation, and complex span plus n>0 proves nonzeroness. S002 applies localization only after verifying Q is the fraction localization of R and proves μ-injectivity by a single nonzero denominator, not by the false inference J⊂C implies rank one. S003 constructs both maps for tensoring the direct decomposition, checks balancing and inverse composites on generators, then obtains n=nr from the registered dimension tools. Since n>0, r=1. S004 uses this dimension to obtain rational coefficients of generators; S005's repeated division terminates on positive integers because p≥2; S006 uses the attained finite minimum to prove both containments J⊆Rb and Rb⊆J. All H/N/M inputs have the stated roles, and the final statement eliminates all generator choices.\",\"source_application_check\":\"At S002 M004 has A=R, B=Q, S=nonzero R and module J; R⊂Q is a domain, fractions give the localization surjectivity, and its injectivity gives the equality condition with multiplier 1. Its denominator property supplies sz=1⊗c, which directly yields the claimed injection of μ. At S003 M001 extends an N002 basis of M_R to Q, M002 gives dimension n, M008 gives Q-freeness of T, F002 gives finite generation, M006 sums the dimensions of n copies of T, and M005 uses the explicitly constructed equivalence. At S004 M003 uses a singleton nonzero vector 1⊗a, nonzero because μ(1⊗a)=a≠0; F002 supplies finite dimension and F003 supplies dimension 1. Its spanning conclusion is exactly what produces the rational coefficients, with no hidden change of scalar field.\",\"declaration_check\":\"T and μ are defined from J in S002 before dimension or injection is claimed; r is defined in S003. F001 precedes the choices a,k,g in S004, and nonzeroness permits discarding zero generators with k≥1. The per-index coefficients in S004 are locally quantified choices from the singleton spanning result; F004 then precedes the actual family q in S005. F005 precedes νs,u in S006, and the finite nonempty index set supplies ν and an attained minimum. b=p^ν a is defined with p≠0 and may initially be viewed in C; only the minimum-generator calculation proves b∈J. The conclusion's universal generator clause is proved without reusing the particular constructed b as an extra assumption.\"},{\"id\":\"R004\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R004 with its explicit H001,H002,H004,N001,N002,N003 inputs. S001 proves the kernel and denominator facts for ρ, uses characteristic p exactly, and proves lattice preservation of h from h=xy-yx. S002 displays both tensor isomorphisms, checks balancing, quotient representative independence and inverse composites; operator intertwining follows on pure tensors. S003 uses the N003 basis and scalar extension to construct β and verifies the reduction basis by coordinates; N001 gives the generator matrices, and N002 gives preservation and the induced matrix units. S004 uses only indices ≤λ, transfers r!X_r=x^r from the lattice, and deduces invariance under every ε_ij from powers, scalars and composition. No algebraic closure or distinct reduced h-weights is assumed, and the witness b is eliminated in the existence/universal basis claims.\",\"source_application_check\":\"M001 at S003 is instantiated with R→K via ρ from F000, module M_R and basis (b e_i) from N003. Its native basis is on K⊗_R M_R; the displayed balanced flip transports it to M_R⊗_R K, and F001 transports it to V(K). Thus no tensor-order identification is silently assumed. M007 at S004 uses d=r and prime p with r≤λ<p from H001. F000's kernel calculation turns p∤r! into its nonzero K-image, justifying each inverse. Binomial inverses come separately from N002's R-unit conclusion through the ring map ρ, not from an unstated mod-p weight condition.\",\"declaration_check\":\"The witness b is introduced from N003 at S001 and remains scoped through S004. ρ and F_p are constructed and verified in S001 before use in tensor extension. F001 precedes β's definition in S003. The basis property of β is established before defining its matrix units ε in the same paragraph. Dummy tensor entries in S002 have the stated domains supplied by their tensor factors and quotient representatives; their balanced formulas define actual maps. All free objects exported by N004 are explicitly bound, and induced X,Y are distinguished in the text from their complex counterparts by scalar extension.\"},{\"id\":\"R005\",\"dependency_and_local_assumption_check\":\"Inspected R005's direct-input statement N004 without using its producer. N004 itself supplies the β basis, matrix-unit action and invariant-subspace consequence, while H001 supplies 0∈I and n>0. L1 is the invariance antecedent; L2 is solely the nonzero branch. F001 establishes the joint nonzero vector/nonzero coordinate choice before S002. The finite coordinate calculation ε_ij w=c_jβ_i is valid, and c_j^{-1} exists since K is a field and c_j≠0. S002 discharges L2 by combining with the zero branch, and S003 discharges L1 and universally quantifies W. H002,H004 justify the lattice action in the equivalent Lie formulation. No use of a complex eigenvalue argument or field algebraic closure remains.\",\"source_application_check\":\"R005 has no direct M/E application. Its sole internal tool N004 explicitly exports both the matrix-unit definition ε_ijβ_k=δ_jkβ_i and the consequence that every x,y-invariant subspace is ε-invariant. The argument instantiates those conclusions with the chosen basis β and arbitrary W under L1. The final equivalence uses D013's abstract Chevalley generator span and their specified actions x,y,h, rather than identifying the Lie algebra with its operator image.\",\"declaration_check\":\"β is a witness from N004, ε is then its defined matrix-unit family, and W is arbitrary. In S002 w and j are chosen jointly from the earlier F001; c is the unique coordinate family given by β. The index i is universally quantified in the matrix-unit calculation and basis spanning conclusion. The branch-scoped w,c,j do not occur in F002 or P. The formal generators of D013 remain abstract, so the λ=0 case does not collapse the meaning of L(K), and both local assumptions have been discharged.\"}] }","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"defer_primary_source","description":"After actual unavailable primary-source access, preserve a complete exact secondary quotation as an explicitly unverified external assumption. The statement must match the quote in a supplied input. Returns the verification record for E.source.verification; this never grants ordinary Audit A PASS.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"source_id":{"type":"string"},"statement":{"type":"string"},"input_id":{"type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"attempts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["source_id","statement","input_id","quote","attempts"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report only a real substantive/suspected mathematical GAP, unavailable source or conflicting original input, with all five located fields. Ordinary unfinished NL0, source registration and JSON bookkeeping are not reports: continue an actual lookup or draft edit. TASK_INCOMPLETE is unavailable for NL0 authoring. Difficulty or a long run is not evidence of a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review. The optional module locator uses dotted syntax (Mathlib.Topology.Basic), never a slash path; omit it if unknown.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"find_library_sources","description":"Search pinned foundational metadata by an exact declaration name or ordinary mathematical terms. Ranked lexical candidates are not a theorem whitelist or an applicability judgment. Selected sources still need explicit M roots and complete checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible. For an existing string optionally supply both start_line/end_line to request up to 250 numbered lines and its complete text_sha256 for replace_lines. A read end beyond the text returns the remaining existing lines and actual range; the start must exist. Edits never clamp their range.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"end_line":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_author_packet","description":"Same-author closing inspection of one structurally valid own conditional inference: exact direct inputs, output, declarations and own proof. No ancestor bodies, extra H, independent reviewer or Audit A feedback.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"inference":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","inference"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_author_checks","description":"Save actual same-author notes and readiness against shared Audit A criteria. Unresolved/not-checked partial notes can be saved, but only complete actual packet inspection with no known issue can release a proof. Open issues persist until explicit located resolutions. No PASS or mathematical verdict is generated; independent Audit A receives none of these notes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"original_context_note":{"type":"string"},"readiness":{"type":"string","enum":["no_known_issue","unresolved","not_checked"]},"open_issues":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"criterion":{"type":"string"},"location":{"type":"string"},"note":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","criterion","location",